From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: usb: host: xhci-plat: auto-detect LPM support under ACPI from HCSPARAMS3

On CIX Sky1 (and other ACPI-described platform xHCI controllers), the
only way XHCI_LPM_SUPPORT currently gets set is when firmware supplies
the "usb3-lpm-capable" boolean device property in xhci_priv_init()'s
property scan. Under ACPI, this property is not supplied, so the
quirk is never set and the driver logs:

  We don't know the algorithms for LPM for this host, disabling LPM.

xhci_plat_quirks() already runs after xhci_gen_setup() has cached the
read-only capability registers (xhci->hcs_params3 is populated at
drivers/usb/host/xhci.c before get_quirks() is invoked), so the
controller's own U1/U2 exit-latency fields are available at the point
this quirk callback runs and can be used as a hardware-capability
fallback when no firmware property was supplied.

Add a fallback in xhci_plat_quirks(): when running under an ACPI
device node and XHCI_LPM_SUPPORT has not already been set via a
property, set it if the controller reports a nonzero U1 or U2 device
exit latency in HCSPARAMS3. This mirrors the equivalent Sky1-Linux
downstream patch and brings the ACPI integration path in line with
what the DT path already gets from "usb3-lpm-capable".

This only affects idle-link power-management behavior (U1/U2 LPM
entry, suspend/resume, and long-running link stability) - it does not
change enumeration, and is not expected by itself to explain
enumeration-time failures such as a hub-depth "set hub depth failed"
or -71 protocol errors, since those occur before USB core aggressively
drives the link into U1/U2. It is a genuine correctness fix (the
capability was always present in hardware but unreported to the LPM
core under ACPI) and should be verified by confirming
"disabling LPM" no longer appears in dmesg after boot.

Signed-off-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Change-Id: I0078000000000000000000000000000000000078
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
@@ -90,6 +90,17 @@ static void xhci_plat_quirks(struct device *dev, struct xhci_hcd *xhci)
 	struct xhci_plat_priv *priv = xhci_to_priv(xhci);
 
 	xhci->quirks |= priv->quirks;
+
+	/*
+	 * For ACPI platform controllers, auto-detect LPM support from
+	 * hardware capability registers. Under DT, usb3-lpm-capable is
+	 * normally supplied as a firmware property.
+	 */
+	if (!(xhci->quirks & XHCI_LPM_SUPPORT) &&
+	    is_acpi_device_node(dev_fwnode(dev)) &&
+	    (HCS_U1_LATENCY(xhci->hcs_params3) |
+	     HCS_U2_LATENCY(xhci->hcs_params3)))
+		xhci->quirks |= XHCI_LPM_SUPPORT;
 }
 
 /* called during probe() after chip reset completes */
